    "reason": "evidence sufficient (proxy gate verdict; the open aspects need proposals): The linked PR [ev-8a56299107e9] makes the one-line note [ev-a641c063f2d6] concrete. The Prometheus metrics in internal/xfn (function runner and cached runner) changed their subsystem from \"composition\" to \"function\", and the internal/engine metrics dropped their \"XR\" prefix [ev-f21bda8d02a1]. The PR is labelled release/breaking-behavior-change, and [ev-53023dfc93fb] says anyone using these metrics must update to the new names, so dashboards or alerts that query the old names stop matching. The evidence does not show the full metric names (the engine metric list is cut off), but the rename rule, the affected metric groups and the consequence are stated clearly enough to write the subject, change, applicability (operators who use these metrics) and consequence.",
